    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **32 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `AUDIT` logger** \u2014 a static `Logger` obtained via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, matching the logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches to.\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line after a successful create** \u2014 immediately after `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` succeeds (so it only fires on a genuine success, past all validation/quota/duplicate rejections), it logs a line containing the three required values:\n\n```java\nAUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n    owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n```\n\nThe owner id, `customerCode` (assigned earlier in the flow) and `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`, whose `toString()` renders the ISO form matching the JSON response) are all included, satisfying `Cp21Tests`' assertion that an AUDIT line contains all three. Placing it after `saveOwner` guarantees the id is populated. No existing behavior changed \u2014 all 32 tests remain green.",
